===Box office records ===
* ''[[Spider-Man: Brand New Day]]'' had the [[List of highest-grossing openings for films#Biggest openings in the United States and Canada|biggest opening weekend ever]] in the United States and Canada with $360 million, outdoing ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' (2019). It also represented the second film to debut with more than $300 million domestically.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gajewski |first=Ryan |date=2026-08-03 |title=Spidey Surprise! ‘Brand New Day’ Lands Top Opening Weekend Ever With $360M, Beating ‘Avengers: Endgame’ |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/spider-man-brand-new-day-opening-record-endgame-box-office-1236662986/ |access-date=2026-08-04 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref>
**The film had the [[List of highest-grossing openings for films#Biggest opening day in the United States and Canada|biggest opening day]] in the United States and Canada with $168 million, overtaking ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' (2019).<ref>{{Cite news |last=Dunn |first=Jack |date=2026-08-01 |title= Box Office: ‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ Breaks Opening Day Record With $168 Million |url= https://variety.com/2026/film/news/box-office-spider-man-brand-new-day-opening-day-record-1236825606/ |access-date=2026-08-01 |work=Variety |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>
**It became the [[List of highest-grossing films in the United States by year|highest-grossing film of all time domestically in the United States and Canada]], surpassing ''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]'' (2015).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rubin |first=Rebecca |date=2026-09-16 |title=‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ Overtakes ‘Star Wars: Force Awakens’ as Highest-Grossing Movie of All Time at Domestic Box Office |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/spider-man-beats-star-wars-biggest-movie-domestic-box-office-1236836593/ |access-date=2026-09-21 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref> [[Lucasfilm]] congratulated the film for beating their record.<ref>{{Cite web |last=O'Grady |first=Sean |date=2026-09-17 |title=Lucasfilm congratulates Spider-Man: Brand New Day on US box office record |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/film/the-force-awakens-star-wars-episode-vii-canada-avengers-press-association-b1297296.html |access-date=2026-09-21 |website=[[The Standard (London newspaper)|The Standard]]}}</ref>
**It crossed the $1 billion worldwide milestone six days after release, becoming [[List of fastest-grossing films|the second-fastest film]] to reach that milestone behind ''[[Avengers: Endgame|Endgame]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=August 4, 2026 |title=Box Office: 'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' Second Fastest To Cross $1B Worldwide |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/box-office-spider-man-brand-new-day-billion-record-1237017056/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260804174406/https://deadline.com/2026/08/box-office-spider-man-brand-new-day-billion-record-1237017056/ |archive-date=August 4, 2026 |access-date=August 4, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>
** It became the 64th film overall to gross $1 billion worldwide.
** The film crossed the $2 billion milestone, surpassing the $1.9 billion gross of ''[[Spider-Man: No Way Home]]'', becoming the highest-grossing [[Spider-Man]] film worldwide and the highest-grossing [[Sony Pictures]] release worldwide. It reached the milestone in 19 days, becoming [[List of fastest-grossing films|the second-fastest film]] to reach that milestone behind ''[[Avengers: Endgame|Endgame]]''.{{cn|date=September 2026}}
** ''Spider-Man: Brand New Day'' became the 8th film to cross the $2 billion mark, the third film to cross the $2.5 billion mark and the [[List of highest-grossing films|third-highest grossing film of all time]].
** In India, it had the biggest opening for a foreign film (surpassing ''Avengers: Endgame'') and became the [[List of highest-grossing films in India|highest-grossing foreign film ever]] (surpassing ''[[Avatar: The Way of Water]]'').<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ramachandran |first=Naman |date=2026-08-10 |title=‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ Becomes Highest Grossing Hollywood Film in India |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/spider-man-brand-new-day-india-box-office-record-1236827437/ |access-date=2026-08-31 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref>
* ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' became the highest grossing movie of all time in October, with the rerelease ''Encore'' making the film surpass ''[[Avatar (2009 film)|Avatar]]'' for the second time. ''Endgame'' initially surpassed ''Avatar ''in July 2019, after which the latter retook the record in March 2021.<ref>{{Cite web|first=Rebecca|last=Rubin|url=https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/avengers-endgame-highest-grossing-movie-ever-avatar-1236894787/|title=‘Avengers: Endgame’ Overtakes ‘Avatar’ as Highest-Grossing Movie in History With $2.925 Billion After ‘Encore’ Re-Release|date=2026-10-04|access-date=2026-10-04 |website=Variety|language=en}}</ref>
* ''[[The Odyssey (2026 film)|The Odyssey]]'' became the [[List of highest-grossing R-rated films|highest-grossing R-rated film]] of all time, surpassing ''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' (2024).<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 August 2026 |title=The Odyssey Worldwide Box Office: Surpasses Deadpool & Wolverine As The Biggest R-Rated Hit Ever! |url=https://www.imdb.com/news/ni65979787/?ref_=ttnw_art_perm |website=[[IMDb]]}}</ref>
** It became the 65th film overall to cross $1 billion worldwide.
** It became [[Christopher Nolan]]'s highest-grossing film worldwide, surpassing ''[[The Dark Knight Rises]]'' (2012).<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=2026-08-09 |title='The Odyssey' Becomes Christopher Nolan’s Highest Grossing Movie Ever At Global Box Office With $1.1B |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/box-office-the-odyssey-christopher-nolan-record-1237029568/ |access-date=2026-08-10 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="RubinOdyssey2026">{{Cite web |last=Rubin |first=Rebecca |date=2026-08-09 |title='The Odyssey' Is Christopher Nolan’s Highest-Grossing Movie Ever With $1.1 Billion and Imax’s Biggest Release of All Time With $289 Million |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/the-odyssey-christopher-nolan-biggest-movie-imax-record-1236830867/ |access-date=2026-08-10 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref>
** It had the highest-grossing opening weekend and the biggest second weekend for Nolan, surpassing ''The Dark Knight Rises''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Naahar |first=Rohan |date=2026-07-30 |title=Christopher Nolan Officially Beats His Own Box Office Record With ‘The Odyssey’ |url=https://collider.com/christopher-nolan-the-odyssey-overtakes-oppenheimer-box-office-727-million/ |access-date=2026-07-31 |website=Collider |language=en}}</ref>
** The film set the record for the highest-grossing opening weekend at [[BFI IMAX]], surpassing ''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi]]'' (2017).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ritman |first=Alex |date=2026-07-31 |title=‘The Odyssey’ Craze Continues as New BFI Imax Screenings Sell Out in Under 30 Minutes (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/global/the-odyssey-new-bfi-imax-screenings-sell-out-30-minutes-1236825096/ |access-date=2026-08-01 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref>
** It became the highest-grossing [[List of films released in IMAX|IMAX release]] of all time, surpassing ''[[Avatar (2009 film)|Avatar]]'' (2009).<ref name="RubinOdyssey2026" /><ref>{{cite news |title=Christopher Nolan’s The Odyssey Triumphs as Highest Grossing IMAX Release of All Time with $289 Million and Counting |url=https://www.imax.com/pr/christopher-nolans-odyssey-triumphs-highest-grossing-imax |access-date=August 11, 2026 |work=www.imax.com |date=August 10, 2026 |language=en}}</ref>
** It became the first [[Motion Picture Association film rating system|R-rated film]] to cross $1.7 billion and became the [[List of highest-grossing films#Highest-grossing films|eleventh-highest grossing film of all time]].
** It became Nolan's highest-grossing film domestically, surpassing ''[[The Dark Knight]]'' (2008).<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=2026-08-23 |title='Spider-Man: Brand New Day' No. 1 $109M WW, 'Insidious' Franchise Rises To $800M WW – Global Box Office |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/global-box-office-spider-man-brand-new-day-insidious-6-1237048315/ |access-date=2026-08-27 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref>
** It became the highest-grossing [[Universal Pictures|Universal]] film ever, surpassing ''[[Jurassic World]]'' (2015).
* The ''[[Toy Story (franchise)|Toy Story]]'' film series surpassed $4 billion with the release of ''[[Toy Story 5]].''<ref>{{Cite web |last=Fuster |first=Jeremy |date=2026-07-26 |title='Toy Story 5' Becomes the Third $1 Billion Film of 2026 |url=https://www.thewrap.com/industry-news/business/toy-story-5-billion-box-office/ |access-date=2026-08-12 |website=TheWrap |language=en-US}}</ref> 
** ''Toy Story 5'' became the highest grossing film of the ''Toy Story'' franchise, surpassing ''[[Toy Story 4]]'' (2019).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Demegillo |first=Manuel |date=2026-08-10 |title=Disney's New 10/10 Sequel Breaks Franchise Record at the Box Office |url=https://movieweb.com/toy-story-5-highest-grossing-sequel/ |access-date=2026-08-12 |website=MovieWeb |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Magazine |first=Animation |date=2026-07-27 |title='Toy Story 5' Tops Billion-Dollar Mark & Takes Year's No. 1 Box Office Spot |url=https://www.animationmagazine.net/2026/07/toy-story-5-tops-billion-dollar-mark-takes-years-no-1-box-office-spot/ |access-date=2026-08-12 |website=Animation Magazine |language=en-US}}</ref>
** It became the 17th [[animated film]] and 63rd overall to cross $1 billion and [[Highest-grossing animated films|tenth-highest grossing animated film]] of all time.
* [[Michael (2026 film)|''Michael'']] became the [[List of highest-grossing biographical films|highest-grossing biopic]] of all time, surpassing ''[[Oppenheimer (film)|Oppenheimer]]'' (2023).<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=2026-06-28 |title=Michael Jackson Movie 'Michael' Becomes Highest-Grossing Biopic Of All Time |url=https://deadline.com/2026/06/box-office-michael-oppenheimer-1236969255/ |access-date=2026-06-29 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Rubin |first=Rebecca |date=2026-06-28 |title='Michael' Surpasses 'Oppenheimer' as Highest-Grossing Biopic With $977 Million Worldwide |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/michael-box-office-record-surpasses-oppenheimer-1236797787/ |access-date=2026-06-29 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref>
** It has the biggest opening weekend for a biopic with $217.4 million grossed worldwide. It also has the biggest opening weekend for a [[Musical film|musical]] biopic.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro|first=Anthony|date=2026-04-26|title=Box Office: 'Michael' Opening to Near $100M U.S, $217M+ WW|url=https://deadline.com/2026/04/box-office-michael-1236870542/|access-date=2026-05-01|website=Deadline|language=en-US}}</ref>
