*''[[Backrooms (film)|Backrooms]]'' became [[A24]]'s biggest opening weekend in its history with $118 million globally.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tassi |first=Paul |title=5 Box Office Records 'Backrooms' Just Broke In One Weekend |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/paultassi/2026/06/01/the-5-box-office-records-backrooms-just-broke-in-one-weekend/ |access-date=2026-06-06 |website=Forbes |language=en}}</ref>
**''[[Backrooms (film)|Backrooms]]'' became A24's highest grossing film to date, overtaking ''[[Marty Supreme]]'' (2025).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galuppo |first=Mia |date=June 7, 2026 |title=Box Office: 'Scary Movie' Stuns With $55M, 'Masters of the Universe' Lands at $29.3M |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/box-office-scary-movie-masters-universe-obsession-backrooms-1236615518/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260607171014/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/box-office-scary-movie-masters-universe-obsession-backrooms-1236615518/ |archive-date=June 7, 2026 |access-date=June 7, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>
**Director [[Kane Parsons]] was 20 years old at the time of the film's release, making him the youngest filmmaker to reach number one at the United States box office. The previous record holder, [[Josh Trank]], was 27 years old when his film ''[[Chronicle (film)|Chronicle]]'' (2012) was released.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Pulver |first=Andrew |date=2026-06-01 |title=Kane Parsons becomes youngest film-maker to open at No 1 in the US with Backrooms |url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/jun/01/kane-parsons-20-youngest-film-maker-no-1-us-backrooms |access-date=2026-06-20 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>
*The [[Moana (franchise)|''Moana'' franchise]] surpassed $2 billion with the release of the [[Moana (2026 film)|live-action remake]] of the [[Moana (2016 film)|original ''Moana'' film]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Coman |first=Monica |date=2026-08-09 |title=Disney's Negative Reviews for $280M Live-Action Remake Addressed by Franchise Star |url=https://www.cbr.com/disney-moana-live-action-negaive-reviews-dwayne-johnson/ |access-date=2026-09-30 |website=CBR |language=en}}</ref>
*The [[Scary Movie (film series)|''Scary Movie'' film series]] surpassed $1 billion with the release of ''[[Scary Movie (2026 film)|Scary Movie 6]]''. It became the first parody film franchise to surpass $1 billion.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-29 |title=SCARY MOVIE Franchise Crosses A Huge Box Office Milestone |url=https://www.fangoria.com/scary-movie-franchise-billion-dollar-box-office/ |access-date=2026-09-30 |language=en-US}}</ref>
*The [[Scream (franchise)|''Scream'' film series]] became the sixth horror film franchise to surpass $1 billion with the release of ''[[Scream 7]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Squires |first=John |date=2026-03-03 |title='Scream' Just Became One of Only Six Horror Franchises to Cross $1 Billion at the Box Office |url=https://bloody-disgusting.com/movie/3938871/scream-just-became-one-of-only-six-horror-franchises-to-cross-1-billion-at-the-box-office/ |access-date=2026-09-30 |website=Bloody Disgusting! |language=en-US}}</ref>
**''Scream 7'' became the highest grossing film in the series, surpassing ''[[Scream (1996 film)|Scream]]'' (1996).<ref>{{Cite web |title=‘Scream 7’ Slashes Past $200 Million at the Global Box Office {{!}} Paramount |url=https://www.paramount.com/news/scream-7-slashes-past-200-million-at-the-global-box-office |access-date=2026-09-30 |website=www.paramount.com |language=en}}</ref>

=== Franchise records ===

* The ''[[Marvel Cinematic Universe]]'' became [[List of highest-grossing franchises and film series|the first franchise]] to surpass $33 billion, $34 billion and $35 billion with the release of ''Spider-Man: Brand New Day'' as well as the rerelease ''Avengers: Endgame Encore''.
* The [[Spider-Man in film|''Spider-Man'' film series]] became the second film franchise to surpass $12 and $13 billion with the release of ''Spider Man: Brand New Day''.

===Other records===
* With 718.6 million views in the first 24 hours and later crossing 1.1 billion, ''[[Spider-Man: Brand New Day]]'' (2026) became the most-viewed trailer of all time, surpassing ''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' (2024).<ref>{{cite news |last1=Moreau |first1=Jordan |title='Spider-Man: Brand New Day' Makes History as First Movie Trailer to Cross 1 Billion Views |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/news/spider-man-brand-new-day-trailer-1-billion-views-first-history-1236697959/ |access-date=26 April 2026|work=Variety |date=24 March 2026}}</ref>

